# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
# Only variables prefixed with NEXT_PUBLIC_ are exposed to the browser.
#
# Leave the Supabase variables blank to run the app in mock mode: every
# repository falls back to in-memory/localStorage data and the app boots with
# no backend at all.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Your Supabase project URL, e.g. https://abcdefgh.supabase.co
# Dashboard -> Project Settings -> Data API
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""

# The *publishable* key (starts with `sb_publishable_`). Despite being public,
# this is safe in the browser: Row Level Security decides what it can read and
# write. Dashboard -> Project Settings -> API Keys
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""

# Human-readable app name surfaced in the UI and document titles.
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_NAME="Studio"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: there is deliberately no SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY here.
#
# The secret (service-role) key bypasses RLS entirely — a leak is total
# database compromise. Nothing in this app needs it: every read and write runs
# as the signed-in user and is authorised by RLS. Admin-only operations are
# expressed as policies (`public.is_admin()`), not as a privileged client.
#
# If you ever add a job that genuinely needs it, put it behind `server-only`,
# keep it out of any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable, and never import it from a module
# that renders user data.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
